{
 "title": "Across 66 OpenNeuro studies, task runs had lower 4-s BOLD autocorrelation than rest runs of the same people; a pre-registered local-coherence decrease did not replicate",
 "abstract": "Across 66 independent OpenNeuro studies, fMRI task runs had a lower autocorrelation of the cortical BOLD signal at a lag of 4 s than rest runs of the same people. This matters because single studies disagree on how tasks change the timing and size of ongoing brain signals, and no study had compared the same within-person contrast across many scanners and task types. We used ReadyNeuro, minimally preprocessed OpenNeuro data. For each person, we subtracted rest-run features from task-run features at the same acquisition repetition time (TR), so scanner, TR and person cancel. Autocorrelation at 4 s is the correlation of a cortical parcel signal (0.008-0.15 Hz) with itself 4 s later; local coherence is the mean correlation between voxels inside a parcel. Studies were split at random into discovery and confirmation halves, and the confirmation tests were written down before the confirmation data were loaded. In 31 confirmation studies (36 people), the 4-s autocorrelation fell by 0.071 (95% CI 0.031 to 0.110; Cohen d -0.66; one-sided p 0.0005; lower in 74% of studies); in 26 discovery studies it fell by 0.080. The rest value is about 0.34. The primary hypothesis, a larger decrease of local than global coherence, held in discovery (d -0.84) but failed in confirmation (d -0.10, p 0.29). In exploratory analyses, the decrease was large for memory, reward, control and story tasks and near zero for working-memory, emotion and block-design sensory tasks, it depended on trial spacing, and it followed changes of the global signal; evoked responses and physiology are therefore leading explanations. Amplitude did not change significantly, but equivalence was not shown. A map of task families from 140 features was at chance in discovery and weakly above chance in confirmation, mostly for films and stories. Limitations: one to three people per study, task labels only, and a confirmation set built partly from shards that were already downloaded.",
