   "path": "files/results/fig1_shift_by_study.png",
   "caption": "Task-minus-rest change per study (same person, same TR), discovery (blue; all 36 extracted studies, 26 at pre-registration) and confirmation (orange; 31 studies), with mean and 95% CI over studies. The 4-s autocorrelation fell in both halves; local coherence and its excess over global coherence fell only in discovery; amplitude did not change significantly. Top: controls (triangle CO2, square sleep, diamond sedation, open circle rest variants)."
  },
  {
   "path": "files/results/fig2_parcel_maps.png",
   "caption": "Mean task-minus-rest change per Schaefer parcel over all study entries of both halves (parcel centroids, axial and sagittal views). Autocorrelation at 4 s fell in all 100 parcels, but parcel changes are strongly correlated (one shared component carries 61%); local coherence fell in 94%."
  },
  {
   "path": "files/results/fig3_by_family.png",
   "caption": "Change of the 4-s autocorrelation and of amplitude by nominal task family, one dot per study and stage; bars are family means per stage. Exploratory: the size of the autocorrelation drop differs by family (Kruskal-Wallis p 0.049)."
  }
